PURPOSE
H55 showed that:
wake,
repair,
scarcity validation,
and
structural probing
can share one abstract active-resource envelope through typed marginal bids plus a small anti-starvation path.

H56 removes the last hidden assumption:

ONE LOGICALLY SHARED GLOBAL TOKEN COUNT.

It asks whether a developmental organism can coordinate active-resource use using only:
- local demand;
- local typed value;
- local neighborhood communication;
- spatially mobile conserved capacity;

without:
- a central scheduler;
- a global active-token counter;
- organism-wide queue state.

H56 also deliberately tests an alternative to economic-style price control:

CONSERVE THE ACTIVATION RIGHT ITSELF.

BOUNDARY
This is synthetic.

It does not:
- freeze a production resource representation;
- prove activation capacity should literally be tokenized;
- freeze the neighborhood transport rule;
- require a grid;
- modify or execute STAB-18-R1.

