DIAGNOSTIC CENTRAL ORACLE
Global oracle sees all demand
and
allocates at most:

20

activation units to the highest-value currently available work.

This is NOT operationally allowed.

It is used only as an upper-bound reference.

COMPARATOR A — ADVISORY DIFFUSED PRICE
Each region maintains a local active-load price.

Price updates from:
local/neighborhood recent activation
relative to a nominal local capacity share.

Price diffuses only to nearest neighbors.

Typed demand activates when:
local bid > local price.

No hard conserved activation object exists.

COMPARATOR B — ACTIVITY-DEPENDENT INHIBITORY FIELD
A shared local inhibitory field:
- rises with local activity;
- diffuses locally;
- decays over time.

Typed demands are suppressed by the inhibitor.

This is a homeostatic / reaction-diffusion-like comparator.

It contains no explicit global cap.

COMPARATOR C — CONSERVED MOBILE ACTIVATION CREDITS
Exactly:

20

activation-credit units exist in the organism.

Initial credits are spatially distributed.

Every step:

1.
cells estimate local typed demand value;

2.
credits may move only to nearest-neighbor regions;

3.
movement follows local unmet-value gradients;

4.
credits are conserved during movement;

5.
a region can activate only as much work as locally held credits permit;

6.
after activation,
credits remain available in that locality for future redistribution.

No global price
or
global active count
is observed.

Primary transport:

8 local movement rounds per synthetic step.

A small four-step structural-access floor is retained from H55.

