ARCHITECTURAL INTERPRETATION
The strongest current cross-modal resource architecture is not:

PURE MARKET PRICE.

It is closer to:

CONSERVED MOBILE CAPACITY

+

LOCAL VALUE / PRICE GRADIENTS

+

TYPED BIDS

+

BOUNDED FAIRNESS / BOOTSTRAP.

Price decides:
where credits are worth moving.

Conservation decides:
whether activation is physically possible.

Fairness decides:
whether slow-return capability can be permanently starved.

